# Visualization Concept — Productive / Cognitive Enhancement / Part 1.0: The Cognitive Architecture

> **Style lock:** Productive pillar · Cognitive Enhancement track · the locked **"Neural Signal Schematic"** style (instrument-grade JetBrains-Mono labels, single-alarm-color discipline, the mind rendered as a signal/power schematic — never a glowing brain). This is the 5th Cognitive concept and the FOUNDATION/MAP article: every later Cognitive poster (4.0 escalation power-supply · 4.1 dual-rail engine board · 4.2 six-channel overdrive console · 4.3 swap patch-bay) is a *zoom-in on one region of this board*. So this poster's job is different from all of them: it is not an operating instrument, it is **the labeled blueprint / legend they all read from.**

---

## 1. The Big Idea

**One sentence:** The reader should feel "*now I have the map*" — the instant where a drawer full of random smart-drug bottles collapses into one labeled board with exactly six sockets, sitting on a base that does 90% of the work.

The emotional beat is the article's own opening line: *"You cannot optimise a system you can't picture."* This poster's only job is to hand the reader the picture — so completely that every compound, every later article, has an obvious home before they read it.

## 2. Visual Metaphor or Structure

**A two-tier labeled motherboard / architectural cross-section — the unpopulated master schematic.** Read as a strata cutaway, top to bottom:

- **SOFTWARE board (top, brightest)** = Cognitive Performance, "the Fit brain · the brain you DEPLOY." Foreground, lit, the dashboard you feel every working hour.
- **HARDWARE board (middle, dimmer/cooler)** = Neural Preservation, "the Healthy brain · the brain you still own at 80." Structural, mostly invisible day-to-day. The software board's power pins plug *down* into it.
- **The 90% BASE PLANE (bottom, dominant by area, glowing)** = sleep, the dopamine environment, training, cognitive-load management. This is the bedrock that actually powers everything above it.

Why this metaphor and not the others in the track: the four application posters are *operating instruments* (you run them). This is the **reference diagram** — software-runs-on-hardware-runs-on-the-base rendered as physical strata. It is the only Cognitive poster where nothing is "switched on" or "running"; instead every socket is an **empty labeled mount** waiting for a compound. That is exactly the article's point — it teaches you the board before a single dose.

## 3. Layout Description

**Orientation: portrait** (the software→hardware→base-plane stack is a vertical cross-section; echoes the vertical-base composition of 4.0/4.1 so it reads as family, but distinguished as a *strata blueprint*, not an instrument).

Top-to-bottom strata:

1. **Headline band** (top).
2. **SOFTWARE BOARD** — the brightest layer, carrying three labeled pathway sockets left→right along a horizontal **EXCITATION ↔ INHIBITION (gas ↔ brakes)** spine:
   - **Drive / Executive** (far gas end) — gas-pedal glyph, `dopamine / norepinephrine`, micro-label "task latency → 0," an example chip *Modafinil* ghosted into the mount to show placement.
   - **Memory & Processing** (centre) — a distinctive **two-port socket**: a FUEL port (choline donor = "fill the tank") and a BRAKE-RELEASE port (AChE inhibitor = "fix the leak"), `acetylcholine`.
   - **Flexibility / State** (far brake end) — a clamp/damper glyph, `GABA / serotonin`, micro-label "quiet the noise so the signal moves," with a small amber note "more stimulation ≠ more flexibility → Part 1.1."
   - A small balance reading on the spine: **"a good brain = gas AND working brakes."**
3. **HARDWARE BOARD** — cooler, dimmer, three sockets:
   - **Neurogenesis** — `BDNF / NGF`, callout "biggest lever isn't a pill — it's cardio" (a thin tie-line out to the Athletic series).
   - **Glutamate / Neuroprotection** — excitotoxicity guard, example chip *Memantine* ghosted in; a **systemic-biomarker strip bolted to its edge** (`hs-CRP · lipids · glucose · BP`) labeled "a brain is a vascular organ."
   - **Neurosteroid Base** — `pregnenolone / DHEA`, enhanced-lifter note "TRT brain fog lives here — not in more test."
4. **THE 90% BASE PLANE** — the largest single element by area, glowing cyan, four feed-pillars rising into both boards: `SLEEP · DOPAMINE ENVIRONMENT · TRAINING · LOAD MANAGEMENT`. Engraved: **"90% of your output."**
5. **The 10% MARGIN taps** — the *only* place chemistry enters: six tiny trim-injection nubs at the socket edges, collectively labeled "chemistry = the 10% margin." The size contrast (vast base plane vs pinprick chem taps) **is** the 90/10 thesis as geometry.

**Docked at the side/foot — two teaching devices:**
- **The placement rail (a "parts bin"):** a scatter of unplaced, dim-grey example chips (*Modafinil · Lion's Mane · Adderall · Memantine · choline · theanine…*) with dotted lines each snapping into exactly ONE of the six sockets — "the drawer stops being random." This is the Pokémon-cards-with-no-map problem getting solved on the page.
- **The SCOREBOARD readout:** a small meter cluster — leading metrics `DEEP-WORK VOLUME` (headline) · `TASK LATENCY` · `COGNITIVE ENDURANCE` + a weekly-PR battery tick — each gauge wired *back to the socket it diagnoses* (task latency → Drive). Law plate: **"MEASURE INPUTS, NOT OUTPUTS · manage the leading, judge by the lagging."**

**Eye path:** headline → the bright software dashboard (what you feel) → down through the hardware you forget → lands on the dominant glowing base plane (the punchline: the base is the real power) → the eye snaps to the parts-bin sorting itself into the six homes → settles on the scoreboard. The composition argues "build downward, measure sideways."

